# ggPSE - Roadmap and TODO

The roadmap summarizes what features are upcoming and some ideas. Roughly ordered by priority within each section.

## v0.3.0
- [ ] split up the profile file in multiple functions
- [ ] `ggPSE_donut()` : widen the color palette 
---

## known issues / technical debt
- [ ] `ggPSE_interactive()` is not well integrated, this needs some refinement
- [ ] `ggPSE_badge()`: the new features like hiearachy do not integrate well. Also the hardcoded ISO country names might need a better solution
  (the table covers only part of the ISO 3166-1 codes; unknown codes are now shown as given).
- [ ] `ggnewscale` (not yet listed in Suggests): when both `value_col` and `highlight` are supplied
  simultaneously, scale conflict occurs - proper fix needs `ggnewscale::new_scale_fill()`
- [ ] `ggPSE_donut()` still has a scale confilct (it fails after a gradient base plot).
- [ ] `ggPSE_donut()` removes all text layers of the plot it receives, including value labels; call `ggPSE_text()` after it.
- [ ] `ggPSE_donut()` uses ggforce: ggforce 0.4.x ignores `linewidth` (the declared minimum is 0.4.0).
- [ ] `ggPSE_bubble()` combined with `ggPSE()`: using both together requires manual legend cleanup 
- [ ] `ggPSE_profile()` has outgrown the function and should be split.
- [ ] `ggPSE_bar()` draws no legend
- [ ] `symbol_position`/`number_position`: the overlap warning was tuned for `base_size = 10` (tiles of about 1 cm)
- [ ] `ggPSE_theme("dark")` is a starting point: tiles without data and the symbol colours keep their light-theme look

---

## ideas / maybe someday
**here realism stops and dreams begin** 
- [ ] adding of brackets to describe certain groups
- [ ] creating a proper dark theme
- [ ] using `ggdensity` package to visualize certain clusters
- [ ] ggPSE_connect(): connect elements in either a "graph-style" or alluvial-style
- [ ] Include oxidation states in the built-in data
- [ ] Publishing on CRAN
- [ ] curated examples with PSE such as NMR-active nuclei, EPR nuclei, (to be continued)
- [ ] `ggPSE_animated` - an experimental feature to animate as gif or mp4
---

## Done

- [x] Initial proof-of-concept script (original research script)
- [x] Rewrote without custom grob machinery - replaced with `geom_tile()` + `geom_text()`
- [x] Core test suite covering all exported functions
- [x] `ggPSE_highlight()` deleted — merged into `ggPSE()` via `highlight` parameter
- [x] `.interp_hex()` moved to `R/zzz.R` as package-level internal helper
- [x] Two datasets: `ggpse_grid` (4 cols) and `ggpse_elements` (17 cols, IUPAC 2021 + NIST)
- [x] NAMESPACE generated via roxygenise()
- [x] Tile border parameter with transparent default
- [x] Per-tile text contrast via WCAG luminance calculation
- [x] Atomic number display in top-left corner via `show_atomic_number`

### v0.1.0 - get it working

- [x] Finalize `ggPSE()` function
  - [x] introduce adaptive colors
  - [x] optimize styling for basic plots
  - [x] fix text overlaps when `show_atom_label = TRUE`
  - [x] add `highlight` parameter for discrete element groups with legend
  - [x] add `tile_border` parameter with auto-detection
- [x] Write `data-raw/prepare_element_data.R` - have option for built-in small data set or periodicsystem bigger data set.
- [x] Change the `ggPSE_highlight()` to a simple highlight option in `ggPSE()`
- [x] Finalize `ggPSE_badge()` - country flags via ggflags, text fallback, up to 3 flags per tile
- [x] Finalize `ggPSE_bubble()` - white tile background, bubble-only signal, NA rows filtered silently
- [x] Finalize `ggPSE_bar()` - in-tile bar encoding, 4 sides, fixed thickness, proportional length
- [x] Write roxygen2 docs for all exported functions
- [x] Run `rcmdcheck::rcmdcheck()` - reach zero errors, zero warnings, zero notes
- [x] Write introduction vignette (`vignettes/getting-started.Rmd`)
- [x] Write a `README.md` with install instructions and a minimal example with output image

---

## v0.3.0 - done so far

- [x] `symbol_position`, `number_position`, `symbol_size`, `symbol_nudge`, `number_nudge` in `ggPSE()` and `ggPSE_interactive()`
- [x] `label_na` (blank tiles without data) and `text_color` (one fixed text colour)
- [x] `ggPSE_text()`: extra text lines per tile from a data column
- [x] categorical `highlight` as a named list of symbol vectors + `highlight_colors`; named colours no longer crash
- [x] `ggPSE_theme()` keeps colour scales and does not modify the plot it receives; `"publication"` redesigned for print
- [x] data checks: element symbols, repeated rows, numeric values; value columns named like tile columns work
- [x] `LazyData`: `ggpse_elements` and `ggpse_grid` available without `data()`
- [x] `ggPSE_bar()`: bars start at zero, `limits` argument
- [x] `ggPSE_badge()`: `badge_size`, unknown ISO codes, warnings for extra flags and missing codes
- [x] colours: `colors`, `midpoint`, `limits`, `breaks`, `labels` in `ggPSE()`/`ggPSE_interactive()`; the text colour is chosen against the colour each tile really gets (also fixes tiles without data and colour changes between animation frames)
- [x] `text_color` can name a column of `data` (one colour per element)

---

## v0.2.0 - updates for usecases

### new features
- [x] zooming for subsets of data
- [x] `ggPSE_donut()` - doughtnut/pie chart per tile showing supply mix by country
- [x] `ggPSE_profile()`: Showing trendlines over periods or groups incl f-block
- [x] `ggPSE_save()`: wrapper for ggsave
- [x] update `ggPSE_badge()`: add sizing of the flags as another parameter to create a sort of hierarchy.
- [x] `ggPSE_sparkline()` - mini chart per tile for time-series data (experimental)
  - [x] sparkbar: A per-tile bar chart displaying continous values.
  - [x] Make sparkline and sparkbar experimental features
  - [x] Documentation of the experimental features
- [x] Fix group line ordering bug in `ggPSE_profile()`
- [x] Add `ggPSE_theme()` - a few pre-built theme variants (minimal, dark, publication)
- [x] Change to MIT license
- [x] pkgdown site setup  

### interactivity

- [x] Add `ggPSE_interactive()` wrapper using `ggiraph`
  - Tooltip content configurable via a `tooltip_cols` argument
- [x] Test `ggiraph` output in Quarto HTML documents
- [x] Test `ggiraph` output in Shiny

